1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,840
 I'll never forget a Saturday almost 20 years ago.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:08,840
 I had just been called into a stake presidency, and I hadn't yet been released as bishop.

3
00:00:08,840 --> 00:00:12,680
 We had five young children, a business to run and a full day of church meetings starting

4
00:00:12,680 --> 00:00:15,800
 at 8 a.m. and concluding with the War of Temple Night.

5
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:19,960
 It was a busy time and I wanted to give my all to the Lord, but I was never sure if I

6
00:00:19,960 --> 00:00:22,160
 had enough to give.

7
00:00:22,160 --> 00:00:26,000
 At a midday leadership meeting, the presiding authority invited questions.

8
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:30,480
 I gathered my courage and asked a question about an administrative matter that was troubling

9
00:00:30,480 --> 00:00:31,480
 me.

10
00:00:31,480 --> 00:00:36,360
 Instead of getting a hopeful answer, I felt like my question was dismissed.

11
00:00:36,360 --> 00:00:39,380
 I felt a little disheartened and unappreciated.

12
00:00:39,380 --> 00:00:44,320
 I questioned why I was sacrificing so much if I was going to feel this way.

13
00:00:44,320 --> 00:00:48,360
 I left that meeting with no desire to attend the War of Temple Night.

14
00:00:48,360 --> 00:00:52,760
 I called my wife, told her how discouraged I was, and said, "Let's go to dinner instead

15
00:00:52,760 --> 00:00:54,440
 of the temple."

16
00:00:54,440 --> 00:01:00,240
 Lindsay wisely responded, "No, I think you need to be in the temple we'll talk after."

17
00:01:00,240 --> 00:01:04,520
 So I went to the temple, but not with the best attitude.

18
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:09,680
 As I entered the dressing room, rumbling to myself, I heard someone say, "How are you,

19
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:11,520
 brother?"

20
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:17,000
 It was the other day on eight jokes.

21
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,220
 We had never met before, and I wasn't about to tell a member of the corner of the 12 apostles

22
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:23,420
 how discouraged I felt.

23
00:01:23,420 --> 00:01:27,780
 So I forced a smile and said, "Everything's great."

24
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:31,540
 I changed into my temple clothes, and as I walked out to my surprise, the other oaks

25
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:34,340
 was waiting for me.

26
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:40,060
 He said, "Brother, tell me how you are really doing.

27
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:43,820
 Something about the compassion in his voice helped me open up."

28
00:01:43,820 --> 00:01:50,500
 The other oaks listened, expressed sincere gratitude, said some encouraging words, and

29
00:01:50,500 --> 00:01:53,740
 He even answered my administrative question.

30
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:58,940
 Then he gave me a big hug, and in an instant I went from feeling like giving up to feeling

31
00:01:58,940 --> 00:02:03,420
 like I could give my whole soul in service to the Lord.

32
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:07,060
 Five years later, my wife and I were invited to meet with Elder Oaks in his office.

33
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:12,420
 I can imagine my excitement, excited to reminisce about the experience we had shared.

34
00:02:12,420 --> 00:02:16,860
 I asked him, "Do you remember the conversation we had in the temple?"

35
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:20,760
 I don't think so," he said.

36
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:25,900
 Have we met before?

37
00:02:25,900 --> 00:02:30,980
 I recounted the experience and reminded him how his act of compassion had lifted my spirits

38
00:02:30,980 --> 00:02:33,820
 and changed my life.

39
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:37,300
 The other oaks responded, "I'm sorry, brother, I don't remember that."

40
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:45,740
 Then sensing my disappointment, he added, "But it's what we do, isn't it?"

41
00:02:45,740 --> 00:02:53,740
 words of state at the ever since. That is what we do. As covenant followers of Jesus Christ,

42
00:02:53,740 --> 00:03:00,640
 we minister with compassion to whomever God places in our path. We do it because that's

43
00:03:00,640 --> 00:03:06,500
 what the Savior did. And we've made a covenant to follow Him. Each Sabbath day, when you and

44
00:03:06,500 --> 00:03:07,680
 and I partake of the sacrament.

